// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
; specs/fpga/wasm_board_ax7203.t27 -- a WASM-executing cell on the ALINX AX7203, one spec
; Board phase (P1) of the epic gHashTag/trinity-fpga#917: AI-generated FPGA hardware that
; executes WASM. Everything between the UART pins is this file; the RTL is generated by t27c
; and never hand-written. The only foreign Verilog in the build is the board top that supplies
; the STARTUPE2 config-oscillator clock and the pins, flagged for the owner label
; owner-approved-foreign on the pull request; the XDC is the existing gf16_clean_ax7203.xdc,
; reused byte for byte.
; -
; WHY. The MVP spec specs/fpga/wasm_interp.t27 proved the interpreter as executable t27: 23
; opcodes, 16 real WASM bodies, 25 checks, icarus green, but no ports and no clock. This cell
; puts that engine on silicon: the same one-opcode-per-clock execution, reached through a real
; UART, on a real board, checked against a golden fixed before the run.
; -
; THE MACHINE. One clock does one thing: a piece of one UART frame, or one WASM opcode. The
; tick body step_all is a plain fn (a task in the generated Verilog, drivable from the tests)
; and on_clock wraps it for the ports. The task keeps blocking assigns, so the tests in this
; file and the silicon clock run the identical sequential body; the sections are ordered so
; every strobe (rxnew, frame_go) is consumed one tick after it is produced. The engine is the
; Verilog-lowerable subset: u32 scalars, u8 bytes, indexed array reads and writes, flat
; if/else opcode dispatch, no loops in the tick body. Programs are the straight-line bodies of
; the MVP, byte for byte; if/else and br need a label stack and stay a separate increment.
; THE ALU HAS ONE HOME. The 24 single-clock i32 ALU opcodes (the ten compares, add, sub, the
; eight bitwise/shift/rotate bytes, eqz, clz, ctz, popcnt) are not 24 hand-copied branches:
; alu_arity(op) says how many operands a byte pops (0 = not an ALU byte) and alu_eval(op, a,
; b) is the value it pushes, each written once below. The tick takes one arm for all 24, and
; specs/fpga/wasm_opcodes.t27 `use`s this module and calls the same two functions as its
; oracle, so the table's expected values and the silicon's cannot be two different algorithms
; (issue #12011). The direction is forced: t27c gen-verilog imports only enums and structs
; from a used module, never a function body, so the bodies live in the module that is lowered.
; P2 widens the set: multi-byte signed LEB for i32.const (an operand-fetch submachine in the
; shape of the mul microsequence), drop, select, the unsigned compares, clz/ctz/popcnt,
; shr_u, rotl/rotr, and div/rem signed and unsigned (a 32-clock restoring divider), plus the
; program store loaded over the wire. The MVP spec keeps proving what this cell does not run.
; -
; P6 DESIGN FLOOR (2026-10-25), the architectural increment after P5 (the label stack,
; in flight as #12010/#12011): the 64-bit datapath, law before silicon. Today st[] and
; the answer register res are 32-bit, so i64.const and f64.const land wholesale only as
; far as their low half -- the honest boundary the P3/P4 comments above record. This
; floor is the design that removes it, stated where it will be executed and tested where
; it can be tested today, in simulation, without silicon and without touching one
; executable line.
; STACK_2x32. Every logical stack slot becomes TWO u32 words: slot k's low word at
; st[2k] (st_lo) and its high word at st[2k+1] (st_hi), little-endian word order to
; match the wire's little-endian byte order. sp counts words: a push adds 2, a pop
; removes 2, so sp is even forever (the parity invariant); underflow is sp < 2,
; overflow is sp + 2 > STACK_WORDS. Slots are UNIFORM: an i32 or f32 value occupies
; the lo word with hi zero, an i64 or f64 value occupies both -- one slot shape for
; every type, so sp arithmetic never depends on the type sitting on the stack. The
; physical array doubles, 16 words to STACK_WORDS = 32, keeping STACK_MAX = 16 as the
; LOGICAL depth it already names; the live dispatch below still runs the one-word
; model until the silicon increment migrates it.
; I64.ADD = TWO ADDS + ONE CARRY. The opcode byte is 0x7C (pinned by the t27b
; emitter's law, specs/tri/t27b/wasm.t27, the i64 stack floor). The compute law:
; lo = add64_lo(a_lo, b_lo) -- verbatim today's i32.add; c = add64_c(a_lo, b_lo) --
; a single bit, the u64-widened low sum crossing 0xFFFFFFFF; hi = add64_hi(a_hi,
; b_hi, c) -- the second add absorbs the carry, and a carry OUT of the high add is
; dropped, wraparound, the same law i32.add already follows at 32 bits. Silicon
; shape: two shallow conditional 32-bit adds, the second with carry-in, the same
; cone i32.add already closes inside the phase-gated 34.3 MHz engine bar -- no
; microsequence, unlike mul and div. With two-word slots, i64.const's SLEB128
; submachine assembles into both words (the ERR_LEB continuation boundary moves
; outward to i64's ten bytes) and f64.const lands wholesale: eight bytes, one slot.
; THE TWO-WORD ANSWER: OP_RUN_USER64. Chosen over a high-word register + one read,
; because WORD_BITS = 24 is a property of the FIVE-BYTE frame, not of the silicon:
; a hi-register read through that frame could never express more than 24 of the
; high word's 32 bits -- 48 of 64 answer bits observable -- while claiming
; bit-exactness. OP_RUN_USER64 = 0xFC instead: a request byte for byte identical to
; OP_RUN_USER, answered RESP_OK SEQ w0..w7 -- 10 bytes, BOTH answer words in full,
; low word first, little-endian. The answer register becomes the pair (res, res_hi);
; an i32 answer keeps res_hi = 0 by the uniform-slot law, so every 5-byte response
; stays byte-identical and old hosts and vectors see no change. WITNESS
; CONSEQUENCE: the die witness inside the t27os receipt (runs/<sha>.json, the
; receipt that follows a merged die witness, specs/t27os/receipt_result.t27) records
; response bytes, so with the 10-byte frame it can carry i64 answers bit-exactly --
; all eight bytes -- where today's answer carries only the low 24 bits.
; The p6 tests below are SIMULATION LAW: they prove the carry arithmetic, the slot
; addressing and the frame layout in test-report today, the sweep against an
; independent no-overflow reference model; they claim nothing about silicon until
; the datapath increment lands and the fleet crossing runs it on the die.
; -
; THE WIRE. The TRI-NET node link, the one that carried 1035886/1035886 TNF16 requests and
; 251616/251616 mxdot4 requests at 1144744 baud with none lost: CFGMCLK between 65.6 and
; 68.7 MHz, divider 60, one start bit, 8 data bits LSB first, one stop bit.
;   Request  SYNC0 SYNC1 OP SEQ SA SB A0..A15 B0..B15            38 bytes
;   OP is a program id, SEQ is echoed, SA SB and A4..A15 B4..B15 are zero, and the operands
;   are x = A0..A3 little-endian and y = B0..B3 little-endian, both raw u32 with no range
;   limit: the LEB range limits only constants inside program bodies.
;   Response RESP_OK SEQ y0 y1 y2                                5 bytes
;   The word on the wire is the low 24 bits of the u32 result, little-endian. The engine is
;   full 32-bit inside; 24 bits is the response width of this link. Board vectors come in two
;   kinds: exact vectors, whose full result already fits the word, and low-24 vectors (the
;   wraparound and the negative-constant programs), where the golden is the low 24 bits of the
;   full u32 and full-width exactness stays pinned by the MVP spec in simulation.
;   An unknown OP or any engine error (bad opcode, stack underflow or overflow, local index,
;   LEB continuation, program counter past end) answers RESP_BADOP SEQ 0 0 0.
; -
; WHAT A PASS SAYS. This RTL receives real WASM program ids and operands over a UART, executes
; one WASM opcode per clock, and answers with the exact result, on this board, for every
; vector listed here, against a golden built by the host runner from the same program bytes.
; WHAT IT DOES NOT SAY. Nothing about speed beyond one opcode per clock, nothing about
; programs outside the straight-line subset, and nothing about formats: the response word is
; 24 bits by the wire, not by the engine.
; ASCII only, English only.

module fpga_wasm_board;

pub const KIND : str = "board-cell";
pub const ID : str = "fpga/wasm_board_ax7203";
pub const EPIC : str = "gHashTag/trinity-fpga#917";

; --- Board ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const BOARD : str = "ALINX AX7203";
pub const PART : str = "xc7a200tfbg484-2";
pub const IDCODE : u32 = 325279891;
pub const TOP : str = "wasm_board_ax7203";
pub const XDC : str = "trinity-fpga specs/fpga/constraints/gf16_clean_ax7203.xdc";

; --- Wire, the TRI-NET node link (tnf16_on_board_ax7203.t27, mxdot4_on_board_ax7203.t27) --
pub const UART_SOURCE : str = "self; the receiver and transmitter are this spec";
pub const BAUD_DIV : u32 = 60;
pub const HOST_BAUD : u32 = 1144744;
pub const CP2102N_REF_HZ : u32 = 24000000;
pub const CP2102N_N : u32 = 21;
pub const WIRE_BAUD : u32 = 1142857;
pub const CFGMCLK_MIN_HZ : u32 = 65600000;
pub const CFGMCLK_MAX_HZ : u32 = 68700000;

; --- Frame ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const SYNC0 : u8 = 170;
pub const SYNC1 : u8 = 85;
pub const RESP_OK : u8 = 165;
pub const RESP_BADOP : u8 = 229;
pub const REQ_BYTES : u32 = 38;
pub const BODY_BYTES : u32 = 36;
pub const RESP_BYTES : u8 = 5;
pub const WORD_BITS : u8 = 24;
; P6 design floor: OP_RUN_USER64's response is 10 bytes -- RESP_OK, SEQ, then BOTH
; answer words little-endian (8 bytes). WORD_BITS = 24 stays the width of the FIVE-byte
; frame; the 64-bit frame answers in full. Every other response keeps RESP_BYTES = 5.
pub const RESP64_BYTES : u8 = 10;
pub const X_OFF : u32 = 4;
pub const Y_OFF : u32 = 20;

; --- P2 wire program store: OP_LOAD_PAGE writes a page of code, OP_RUN_USER runs from it
pub const OP_LOAD_PAGE : u8 = 0xFE;
pub const OP_RUN_USER : u8 = 0xFD;
pub const CODE_PAGES : u32 = 4;
pub const PAGE_BYTES : u32 = 32;
; P6 design floor (2026-10-25): OP_RUN_USER64 runs the loaded program like OP_RUN_USER
; -- a request byte for byte identical -- but answers BOTH answer words: RESP_OK SEQ
; w0..w7, 10 bytes, low word first. Not yet in the executed set; the dispatch arm and
; the widened txq land with the datapath increment. 0xFC is the next special below
; OP_RUN_USER (0xFD) and OP_LOAD_PAGE (0xFE); program ids stay 0..PROGS-1.
pub const OP_RUN_USER64 : u8 = 0xFC;

; --- Machine ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
pub const STACK_MAX : u32 = 16;
pub const LOCALS : u32 = 4;
pub const CODE_BYTES : u32 = 101;
pub const CODE_PAD : u32 = 128;
pub const I32_MASK : u64 = 0xFFFFFFFF;
; P6 design floor (2026-10-25): the STACK_2x32 constants, law before silicon. SLOT_WORDS
; is the words per logical slot; STACK_WORDS is the physical word count the silicon
; increment grows st[] to -- 2 x STACK_MAX by hand, written flat like every other const
; here (STACK_MAX stays the LOGICAL depth it already names, 16 slots, so test
; machine_consts keeps its meaning). The live st stays [STACK_MAX]u32 until that
; increment; the addressing law itself (slot k at 2k, 2k+1) is testable today and is,
; as p6_stack_2x32_addressing.
pub const SLOT_WORDS : u32 = 2;
pub const STACK_WORDS : u32 = 32;

; --- opcodes, WebAssembly MVP final bytes (pinned by test opcode_bytes_are_real_wasm) ----
pub const OP_END : u8 = 0x0B;
pub const OP_RETURN : u8 = 0x0F;
pub const OP_DROP : u8 = 0x1A;
pub const OP_SELECT : u8 = 0x1B;
pub const OP_LOCAL_GET : u8 = 0x20;
pub const OP_LOCAL_SET : u8 = 0x21;
pub const OP_LOCAL_TEE : u8 = 0x22;
pub const OP_I32_CONST : u8 = 0x41;
; P3 (2026-10-24): i64.const joins as the LOW-32 floor. OP_I64_CONST decodes the
; same five-byte SLEB128 submachine as OP_I32_CONST and pushes the same u32 word:
; for every i64 whose low 32 bits are what the answer contract expresses, a
; canonical SLEB of five bytes or fewer exists (the fleet's 987654321 and -5 both
; fit); a longer continuation at imm_cnt == 4 refuses with ERR_LEB, the same honest
; boundary as i32. The 64-bit datapath itself stays a separate increment.
pub const OP_I64_CONST : u8 = 0x42;
; P4 (2026-10-24): the float consts join as RAW-BIT words -- no LEB at all. A real
; wasm f32.const carries its four IEEE-754 bytes little-endian right after the
; opcode, f64.const its eight; the floor pushes those bits as the u32 stack word:
; f32 wholesale, f64 as the low 32 (its first four bytes), the same honest floor
; as i64.const. Float arithmetic and the f64 high half stay a separate increment.
pub const OP_F32_CONST : u8 = 0x43;
pub const OP_F64_CONST : u8 = 0x44;
pub const OP_I32_EQZ : u8 = 0x45;
pub const OP_I32_EQ : u8 = 0x46;
pub const OP_I32_NE : u8 = 0x47;
pub const OP_I32_LT_S : u8 = 0x48;
pub const OP_I32_LT_U : u8 = 0x49;
pub const OP_I32_GT_S : u8 = 0x4A;
pub const OP_I32_GT_U : u8 = 0x4B;
pub const OP_I32_LE_U : u8 = 0x4D;
pub const OP_I32_LE_S : u8 = 0x4C;
pub const OP_I32_GE_U : u8 = 0x4F;
pub const OP_I32_GE_S : u8 = 0x4E;
pub const OP_I32_CLZ : u8 = 0x67;
pub const OP_I32_CTZ : u8 = 0x68;
pub const OP_I32_POPCNT : u8 = 0x69;
pub const OP_I32_ADD : u8 = 0x6A;
pub const OP_I32_SUB : u8 = 0x6B;
pub const OP_I32_MUL : u8 = 0x6C;
pub const OP_I32_DIV_S : u8 = 0x6D;
